<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēlectābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		delecto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>delectable, delightful, agreeable</i> (post-Aug.
			for jucundus, amoenus): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 12, 67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apologi (with festivi),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					2, 29</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 3, 6</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Lact. 6, 4, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 7,
				13</span></i>.—<i>Comp.</i>: tibia questu,
			App. Flor. <i>no.</i> 17.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">delec-tabiliter</span></b> , <i>delightfully</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ac decore depicta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 13, 24, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et feliciter declamare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 15,
					1</span></i>
			.—<i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">delectabilius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. de Don. Persev. 53</span></i>
			.</div>
